You can expand upon the about author section to include some more details on me.

I first got interested in Alien & UFOs when I was 5. Me and my next door friend Cole used to play in my backyard. One time we found a rock that was perfectly semetrical and shaped like the head of an alien. We kept the rock and used to pretend we could summon UFOs with it.

I remember a seeing a scary movie about Aliens my parents watched. I was peeping in from the stairwell above and saw an alien crawl inside someones space helmet and eat their face. Terriying. That was my next encounter with the subject of aliens.

As a child the local library used to hold summer book clubs for children. The #1 book theme that appealed to me was Aliens. The first ever book on aliens I read was: Aliens by Don Wullfson (cross reference details about his stories into this section).

I read all kinds of books on aliens including historical record of UFOs but mostly stories. Aliens by Don Wullfson appealed to me because it was decribing things unlike any other I had heard before and I was hooked.

